# state: first-run   (recorded on a disk with no save for the title (NOTES.md E); lane.savestate433)
# Crash Bandicoot: The Wrath of Cortex (56550003). No profile step: NEW GAME
# is always the first item and asks only for a name. Original route PLAYED by
# nav.py on the Nova, 2026-09-29 19:43 PDT (lane.titleroutes session 37, HELD;
# nav session crash-wrath-of-cortex.first-run-20260929T194316); REPLACED
# 2026-10-12 (#433 step 6d): session 46's mark audit found the fixed-timing
# opening's mark landing on the LOAD/SAVE menu, not the warp room hub, on
# replay (result 1-1790757193-lane.hddcrash-1697566, frame 101704). `drive
# generic` replaces the boot-to-hub timing guess with the trained classifier,
# so the mark is confirmed play, not a wait that can drift onto a menu.
#
# Gameplay is the warp room hub, not a level: the stick walked Crash across
# the floor and turned him. The hub is lighter to render than a level, so its
# fps is an upper bound on the title's.
drive generic 300 mark
#
# The play loop walks toward the camera and side to side, and presses no
# button: Crash starts in front of the LOAD/SAVE monitor, and the first
# version of this loop (stick up plus A) walked him back into it and opened
# the Load/Save menu (scratch/replay/crash-wrath-of-cortex-194543/zz-end.png).
axis LY max
wait 1.5
axis LY mid
repeat forever {
    axis LX max
    wait 1.5
    axis LX mid
    axis LY max
    wait 0.5
    axis LY mid
    axis LX min
    wait 1.5
    axis LX mid
    axis LY min
    wait 0.4
    axis LY mid
}
